  "prefLabel": "Env-WC 205.03 Processing of Rulemaking Petitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-WC 205.03 Processing of Rulemaking Petitions.\n\n(a) Upon receipt of a petition to adopt, amend, or repeal a council rule, the council clerk shall forward the petition to the council.\n\n(b) At its first meeting following receipt of a petition to adopt, amend, or repeal a council rule, the council shall review the petition and proceed in accordance with RSA 541-A:4, I.\n\n(c) The petition shall be granted and a rulemaking proceeding shall be initiated if the council determines that the proposed action is:\n\n(1) Consistent with state and federal law and policy; and\n\n(2) Necessary to secure the just, efficient, and accurate resolution of council proceedings in accordance with recognized principles of due process and the requirements of RSA 541-A.\n\nSource. #8977-A, eff 9-14-07",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wc200.html"
